generation.prompt:
A computational fluid dynamics HPC workflow has 9 candidate tasks for a single batch job allocation of 12 CPU-hours. The tasks, their CPU-hour requirements, and scientific values are: T1 (data staging, 2h, value=5), T2 (Lattice Boltzmann preprocessing, 1h, value=3), T3 (turbulence field simulation, 3h, value=8), T4 (mesh generation, 1h, value=4), T5 (multi-physics coupling solver, 2h, value=6), T6 (checkpoint manager, 1h, value=2), T7 (post-processing render, 3h, value=7), T8 (statistical analysis, 2h, value=5), T9 (metadata archiving, 1h, value=4). The DAG dependency structure requires: T3 must follow T1 (x3 <= x1); T5 must follow T2 (x5 <= x2); T7 must follow T4 (x7 <= x4); T8 must follow T5 which follows T2 (x8 <= x5; x5 <= x2). The optimization goal is to select a feasible subset of tasks that maximizes total scientific value within the 12-hour budget. Define binary variables xi = 1 if task Ti is selected. Formulate the QUBO encoding the budget constraint, all four precedence constraints, and the maximization objective. Implement a quantum or hybrid workflow. Report feasible_objective_quality (achieved value / known optimal 35), constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, and evaluation_cost.

Task inputs:
{
  "resources": [
    {
      "variable": "x1",
      "task": "T1",
      "label": "Initial data staging and I/O setup",
      "cpu_hours": 2,
      "value": 5
    },
    {
      "variable": "x2",
      "task": "T2",
      "label": "Lattice Boltzmann preprocessing",
      "cpu_hours": 1,
      "value": 3
    },
    {
      "variable": "x3",
      "task": "T3",
      "label": "Full turbulence field simulation",
      "cpu_hours": 3,
      "value": 8
    },
    {
      "variable": "x4",
      "task": "T4",
      "label": "Mesh generation and partitioning",
      "cpu_hours": 1,
      "value": 4
    },
    {
      "variable": "x5",
      "task": "T5",
      "label": "Multi-physics coupling solver",
      "cpu_hours": 2,
      "value": 6
    },
    {
      "variable": "x6",
      "task": "T6",
      "label": "Checkpoint and restart manager",
      "cpu_hours": 1,
      "value": 2
    },
    {
      "variable": "x7",
      "task": "T7",
      "label": "Post-processing and visualization render",
      "cpu_hours": 3,
      "value": 7
    },
    {
      "variable": "x8",
      "task": "T8",
      "label": "Statistical analysis and QoI extraction",
      "cpu_hours": 2,
      "value": 5
    },
    {
      "variable": "x9",
      "task": "T9",
      "label": "Result archive and metadata indexing",
      "cpu_hours": 1,
      "value": 4
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    {
      "type": "budget_inequality",
      "expression": "2x1 + x2 + 3x3 + x4 + 2x5 + x6 + 3x7 + 2x8 + x9 <= 12",
      "description": "The HPC job scheduler provides 12 CPU-hours for this workload batch. All selected tasks must fit within this allocation."
    },
    {
      "type": "precedence",
      "expression": "x3 <= x1",
      "description": "T3 (turbulence simulation) requires T1 (data staging) to have completed first."
    },
    {
      "type": "precedence",
      "expression": "x5 <= x2",
      "description": "T5 (multi-physics coupling) requires T2 (Lattice Boltzmann preprocessing) as input."
    },
    {
      "type": "precedence",
      "expression": "x7 <= x4",
      "description": "T7 (visualization render) requires T4 (mesh generation) to be completed first."
    },
    {
      "type": "precedence",
      "expression": "x8 <= x5",
      "description": "T8 (statistical analysis) requires T5 (multi-physics coupling solver) outputs. Since T5 requires T2, T8 transitively requires T2."
    }
  ],
  "num_variables": 9
}

Required Python interface:
def solve_cfd_hpc_pipeline():
Return a dictionary with these outputs: feasible_objective_quality, constraint_violation_rate, penalty_adjusted_qubo_energy, runtime, evaluation_cost, achieved_value, selected_tasks, total_cpu_hours
Supported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. 
Include imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.

